mazing job at  absorbing that level of work no problems  whatsoever in order to actually see this  behavior we had to jack the QPS up to  750 and let the test run for over an  hour you can see that over time it takes  a little longer to handle the same  operations for urban IOT the least  invasive fix for this problem was  penned a random prefix to their time  stamps which caused some headaches in  their dashboard for fetching but also  allowed their performance to land back  in the non hot spotted area now I just  want to highlight something again this  is not a standard run-of-the-mill  performance issue it took a couple of  days of really hammering on datastore to  get our test to behave the way that  urban IOT was seeing in the wild and my  guess is that unless your use case is  very similar to theirs chances are you  won't run into it so if you'd like ideas  on where to spend your time instead make  sure you check out the rest of the cloud  performance Atlas content because when  it comes to performance every  millisecond counts
 

